    "competitive_moat": {
     "indicator": "competitive_moat",
     "score": 3,
     "confidence": "M",
     "rationale": "Mixed, segment-dependent picture from FY2025 10-K + market data, not a clean pass on the rubric cross-checks. (a) Pricing power: real but uneven -- Domestic Disney+ ARPU +2.2% (below recent CPI), International ARPU +19% (strong), Parks guest spending +3%. (b) Margin vs. industry median: not evidenced (Entertainment op income +19% on +3% revenue shows leverage but no peer benchmark found). (c) Retention/switching costs: not evidenced beyond strategic intent (Iger calling the Disney+/Hulu bundle \"the strategic moat\"); no churn/retention data gathered. (d) Market share: NEGATIVE for streaming specifically -- Disney+ ~14% US SVOD share, 4th place, explicitly described as trailing Netflix's widening dominance; Parks/IP franchise strength is real but not quantified here. Only 1 of 4 cross-checks (pricing power) has clear positive evidence strong enough to count; rubric requires 2+ for a 4/5. Scored 3 (mild moat, contestable) rather than 4 given the streaming-share evidence actively cuts against, not just fails to support, the case. Sourced from Disney FY2025 10-K (SEC EDGAR, filed 2025-11-13) plus 2026 streaming-market-share industry writeups (evoca.tv, matrixbcg.com) and commentary (Yahoo Finance, Kavout).",
     "source": "manual",
