     "rationale": "FY2025 10-K segment mix (SEC EDGAR, filed 2025-11-13): Linear Networks $9,364M (9.9% of $94,425M total; genuinely contracted -- multi-year MVPD affiliate-fee agreements at contractually specified per-subscriber rates) + Direct-to-Consumer $24,614M (26.1%; recurring subscription revenue, but month-to-month/cancel-anytime, not contracted in the strict sense) = ~36% of company revenue is contracted-or-recurring. Content Sales/Licensing (9.0%) and Experiences (38.3%, mostly transactional ticket/spend) are not visible 12 months out. Sports segment (16.7%, not broken out here) likely has some ESPN affiliate-contract component similar to Linear Networks, which could push the true figure into the 3 band (40-60%) if isolated -- this is a boundary call between bands 2 and 3, scored conservatively at 2 given the Sports-segment split was not available in the evidence gathered. Flag for Alan: worth pulling the Sports segment 10-K detail to firm this up before finalizing.",
